X('documents-required-for-import-into-india',[
 ('Documents for special goods',['Food needs FSSAI registration and often a certificate of analysis. Electronics and many consumer goods need BIS registration. Radio equipment needs a wireless licence, drugs and medical devices need their own licences, and plants and seeds need a quarantine permit. Ask a broker which applies to your product <a href="contact" style="color:#0A6CC2">before you order</a>, and read the guides on <a href="guides/bis-certification-for-imports" style="color:#0A6CC2">BIS</a> and <a href="guides/fssai-import-clearance" style="color:#0A6CC2">FSSAI</a>.']),
 ('Common document mistakes',['Invoice and packing list that show different quantities.','Description on the invoice that is too vague to classify.','Bill of lading that names a different consignee from the importer.','A certificate of origin with the wrong form or an expired date.']),
 ('How to check before you ship',['Send the drafts to your broker. The <a href="document-checker" style="color:#0A6CC2">free document checker</a> also compares the figures across the documents.'])],
 [('Do I need originals or copies?','For clearance most documents are uploaded as scanned copies. Originals of the bill of lading are needed to take delivery from the line, unless it is a telex release or a sea waybill.')])
X('hs-code-classification-general-rules',[
 ('A worked example',['A plastic water bottle with a steel insulating layer. Is it plastic, steel or a household article? The rules look first at the heading text, then at the material that gives the item its essential character, and then at the last heading in numerical order if two still fit. The decision is a judgement, and different officers can differ, so a record of why you chose the code matters.']),
 ('Why classification matters',['It decides the duty, whether a licence or BIS applies, whether anti-dumping duty applies and whether a free trade agreement can be used. A wrong code can mean an unexpected duty demand years later. Use the <a href="customs-duty-calculator" style="color:#0A6CC2">calculator</a> and the <a href="import-duty/" style="color:#0A6CC2">import duty pages</a> to see the rates attached to a code.']),
 ('Getting it right',['Have the full technical description, the material and the use of the product. For a doubtful case, ask for an <a href="guides/advance-ruling-customs-india" style="color:#0A6CC2">advance ruling</a> or ask a licensed broker to confirm the code in writing.'])],
 [('Can two importers use different codes for the same product?','They should not, but they sometimes do. If Customs disagrees with a code, the officer can reclassify it, so keep your supporting documents.')])
X('demurrage-and-detention-explained',[
 ('A simple example',['A container arrives on Monday with five free days at the port. If the cargo is not cleared and gated out by Saturday, demurrage starts on the sixth day at the line’s tariff, and rises in steps the longer it stays. If the empty container is then not returned within the detention free days, detention is added. The tariff is set by the line or the terminal, so ask for it before booking.']),
 ('How to reduce the risk',['File the bill of entry early so clearance does not start at arrival.','Book the truck or rail slot before the cargo lands.','Ask for extra free days when you book, especially for slow lanes.','Know who pays under the contract and the Incoterm, and keep proof of every day of delay.']),
 ('If you are already charged',['Ask for the calculation and the dates. If the delay was caused by the port, customs or the line, you may have a case for waiver, so gather the proof before you pay.'])],
 [('Is demurrage charged on weekends and holidays?','Often yes, unless the tariff says otherwise. Read the line’s terms.')])
X('bill-of-lading-explained',[
 ('What to check on a draft bill of lading',['Shipper, consignee and notify party, exactly as in the sales contract and the letter of credit.','Description of the goods and the number and weight of the packages, matching the invoice and packing list.','Port of loading and port of discharge, vessel and date.','Freight prepaid or collect, as agreed.','Number of originals issued, usually three.']),
 ('Why errors are costly',['A mistake can mean the bank refuses the documents, or the consignee cannot take delivery, or the customs filing does not match. Fixing it after the vessel sails needs an amendment, a fee and time. Review the draft the day you receive it. See the guides on <a href="guides/house-bill-of-lading-vs-master-bill-of-lading" style="color:#0A6CC2">house and master bills</a> and <a href="guides/telex-release-and-surrendered-bill-of-lading" style="color:#0A6CC2">telex release</a>.'])],
 [('Who holds the original bill of lading?','The shipper receives the set from the carrier or forwarder, and sends it to the buyer or the bank, depending on the payment terms.')])
X('airway-bill-mawb-hawb-explained',[
 ('Reading an airway bill',['The airway bill number has 11 digits: a three-digit airline prefix, then eight digits. The prefix identifies the airline, so you can tell the carrier from the number. The bill also shows the shipper, consignee, airports, flight, pieces, weight, chargeable weight and rate.']),
 ('Tracking and labels',['Use the <a href="tracking/" style="color:#0A6CC2">free tracking pages</a> to follow a flight, the <a href="air-cargo-status-codes" style="color:#0A6CC2">status codes guide</a> to read it, and the <a href="awb-label-generator" style="color:#0A6CC2">AWB label generator</a> to print labels.']),
 ('An airway bill is not a title document',['Unlike a bill of lading, a non-negotiable airway bill does not control who owns the goods. It is a receipt and a contract of carriage, and the cargo is delivered to the named consignee.'])],
 [('What is a house airway bill?','A forwarder issues a house airway bill to the shipper for a consolidated shipment, while the airline issues the master airway bill to the forwarder.')])
X('import-export-code-iec',[
 ('Mistakes to avoid',['Applying with mismatched names between the PAN, the bank account and the application.','Forgetting the annual update, which can make the code inactive.','Using an old address that no longer matches the GST registration.','Starting to import or export before the code is issued.']),
 ('After you have the code',['Add it to your invoices and your bank records, link your authorised dealer bank, and register on the customs portal. Then you can file the first bill of entry or shipping bill. A broker can help with the next steps, see <a href="customs-clearance-india" style="color:#0A6CC2">customs clearance in India</a>.'])],
 [('What does the IEC cost?','There is a government fee on application and none for the annual update, though the fee can change. Check the portal for the current amount.')])
X('express-courier-vs-air-freight',[
 ('How to decide',['Courier suits small, urgent parcels, samples and documents, with door-to-door delivery and tracking included. Air freight suits heavier consignments, where the per-kg rate is far lower and you accept an airport-to-airport move with separate clearance. The crossover is usually in the tens of kilograms, but it depends on the lane.']),
 ('Customs differences',['Courier imports into India pass through a simplified clearance up to a value limit, and above it a normal bill of entry applies. See the <a href="guides/courier-import-into-india" style="color:#0A6CC2">courier import guide</a>. Air freight always uses the normal process, so allow time for it.'])],
 [('Can I send commercial goods by courier?','Yes, subject to the value limit and the rules for the product. Some goods cannot go by courier, so check first.')])
X('container-types-explained',[
 ('Choosing the right container',[('table',['Container','Use'],[['20 ft general purpose','Dense, heavy cargo such as tiles, metals, machinery'],['40 ft general purpose','Light, bulky cargo such as furniture, textiles'],['40 ft high cube','Same as 40 ft, with extra height'],['Reefer','Cargo that needs a set temperature'],['Open top, flat rack','Over-height or over-width cargo']],'')]),
 ('How to check the fit',['Enter your cartons or pallets in the <a href="container-load-planner" style="color:#0A6CC2">free 3D load planner</a> to see how many fit, and how heavy the load is. Check the maximum payload with the line, because a 20 ft box often reaches its weight limit before it is full.'])],
 [('What is a TEU?','A twenty-foot equivalent unit. A 20 ft container is 1 TEU and a 40 ft container is 2.')])
X('customs-examination-and-out-of-charge',[
 ('What an officer may look at',['The documents, the goods against the documents and the classification. Depending on the risk, the officer can ask for more papers, order a physical check, or draw samples for testing. A test report can take days, and the cargo waits meanwhile.']),
 ('How to prepare',['Keep the invoice, packing list, certificates and product literature ready. Make sure the cargo is easy to open and reseal, and that your broker or an authorised person attends. A well-prepared examination is usually quick.']),
 ('Out of charge',['Once the officer is satisfied and the duty is paid, the out of charge order is given. The cargo is then released from the custodian against the delivery order. See <a href="guides/bill-of-entry-explained" style="color:#0A6CC2">bill of entry</a>.'])],
 [('Who bears the cost of examination?','The importer, through handling and labour charges at the custodian, and the cost of any test. A mismatch found at examination can also lead to duty or penalties.')])
X('bis-certification-for-imports',[
 ('How to plan for BIS',['Find out whether your product is under the compulsory registration scheme, and whether your overseas factory is already registered. Registration takes time and needs testing in an approved lab, so start before you order in volume. A product that arrives without the registration can be held, sent back, or in some cases destroyed.']),
 ('What the importer must show',['The registration number of the manufacturer, the standard mark on the product and packaging, and the documents that Customs asks for at clearance. Our desk can check the rule for your product, see <a href="customs-brokerage" style="color:#0A6CC2">customs brokerage</a>.'])],
 [('Is BIS needed for samples?','Sometimes there are exemptions for samples and R&D imports, with conditions. Check before you ship.')])
